Every target's prerequisite is `check-go` (pre-existing) or nothing. The
spurious dependency attempt 4 introduced is gone: `release:` (line 306) and
`release-snapshot:` (line 301) have NO prerequisites, and `clean:` (line 148)
has none either -- attempt 4's `clean: check-node` string-concatenation hazard
no longer exists.
Non-test targets, node absent:
  make build       exit 0 (built ./budget2)
  make vet         exit 0
  make -n clean            -> rm -f budget2 / rm -rf dist / go clean   (rc 0)
  make -n dev              -> go run ./cmd/server                      (rc 0)
  make -n install-go       -> curl+untar recipe                        (rc 0)
  make -n release-snapshot -> goreleaser release --snapshot --clean    (rc 0)
  make release             -> "Error: version not specified..." exit 1 (its own
