I used `make -n` for clean/dev/install-go/release deliberately: running them
for real would delete build outputs, start a server, overwrite a Go toolchain
or push a tag. The dry runs show the full recipe text, which is what "does not
require node" needs.
There is no `install` target in this Makefile (only `install-go`); .PHONY line
73 confirms the target list.

